<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Loretta of Sponheim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1300–1346</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Loretta of Sponheim was a countess who governed the Rear County of Sponheim as regent for her young son after her husband's death in 1323. To defend her rights against Archbishop Baldwin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a>, she seized him in 1328 as he travelled on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> and held him at her castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/starkenburg">Starkenburg</a> until he agreed to a favourable settlement.</p></div>
